# Walkthrough - Two-Agent Query Parser Architecture

## Summary
Implemented a production-grade two-agent architecture that separates **query understanding** from **response generation**.

## Architecture Flow
```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[User Query] --> B[Parser Agent]
    B --> C[Query Builder]
    C --> D[Database]
    D --> E[Advisor Agent]
    E --> F[Response + Chart]
```

## Files Created/Modified

### [NEW] [queryParserAgent.js](file:///c:/Users/KHALID/Downloads/HouseHold%20Budgeting/backend/src/agents/queryParserAgent.js)
AI-powered query parser that extracts:
- Date ranges with intelligent parsing ("this year" vs "last year")
- Category/type/merchant filters
- Visualization preferences
- Grounding (web search) requirements

### [NEW] [queryBuilder.js](file:///c:/Users/KHALID/Downloads/HouseHold%20Budgeting/backend/src/utils/queryBuilder.js)
SQL query builder that:
- Converts parsed metadata to PostgreSQL queries
- Builds RAG context from transactions
- Pre-calculates chart data (monthly/weekly totals)

### [MODIFIED] [advisorAgent.js](file:///c:/Users/KHALID/Downloads/HouseHold%20Budgeting/backend/src/agents/advisorAgent.js)
Refactored to:
- Remove all regex-based parsing (~200 lines removed)
- Integrate Parser Agent and Query Builder
- Include parsed query metadata in Opik traces

## Key Improvements

| Feature | Before | After |
|---------|--------|-------|
| "this year" parsing | ❌ Treated as "last 365 days" | ✅ Jan 1 → Today |
| Month names | ❌ Regex with edge cases | ✅ AI understands context |
| Chart selection | ❌ Limited heuristics | ✅ AI-detected intent |
| Grounding | ❌ Pattern matching | ✅ AI-detected need |

## Testing

Try these queries:
```
✅ "Show me this year's spending"
✅ "Compare December and January"
✅ "Grocery breakdown per week"
✅ "Best SIP plans in India"
```

Check Opik for:
- `queryParserAgent.parseQuery` trace
- `advisorAgent.getFinancialAdvice` trace
